{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>YHWH, I heard your report</b>: The sense is that HaShem informed him of the matter of the famine." "And the sense of <b>your deed</b> is that Israel shall live in the midst of these years. And R. Judah said: 'I heard your mights and now revive your deed,' as though it were dead. This is far-fetched." "<b>In the midst of years make known</b> your deed — what He will do, and they are Israel and they are your agents." "<b>In wrath</b>: at the time of wrath, when we are in fear." "<b>Compassion you remember</b>: your compassions. And the word רחם is singular, for רחמים is plural. And R. Moses said: 'In wrath, have compassion and remember the time that You came, You the God, from the south.' This is long and is not correct. And some say: for רחם is a noun, like אהבה, 'I love you, O YHWH, my strength.'"], :book :habakkuk, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 3, :register {:flags {4 ["God"]}}, :notes {4 "The verse alluded to is Judges 5:4 (Deborah's song); 'from the south' renders מתימן per the Song of Deborah. Ibn Ezra calls the interpretation 'long' (i.e., stretches the text too far)."}, :source-witnesses [["<b>Ibn Ezra on Habakkuk</b>- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/havakuk"] ["Ibn Ezra on Habakkuk -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/havakuk"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:49:15.603853704Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}